{
  "model": "blog.blogpost",
  "pk": 1,
  "fields": {
    "title": "Architecting Decoupled Next.js 15 & Django REST APIs for Scale",
    "slug": "architecting-decoupled-nextjs-and-django-apis",
    "content": "Building high-performance web platforms requires a clean separation of concerns. In this article, we explore the architectural decisions behind coupling Next.js 15 App Router with a stateless Django REST Framework (DRF) backend.\n\n### Key Architectural Tenets\n1. **Stateless JWT Authentication**: Keeping session state out of the database tier enables seamless horizontal scaling across instances.\n2. **Reverse Proxying and SSL Termination**: Utilizing Nginx and Cloudflare for SSL offloading and rate limiting.\n3. **Database Connection Pooling**: Preventing connection exhaustion when connecting serverless frontends to PostgreSQL.\n\nWhen properly decoupled, each layer can be optimized, deployed, and scaled independently without bottlenecks.",
    "created_at": "2026-09-17T12:44:18.068Z"
  }
},
{
  "model": "blog.blogpost",
  "pk": 2,
  "fields": {
    "title": "Network Engineering Principles Every Backend Developer Should Know",
    "slug": "network-engineering-principles-for-backend-devs",
    "content": "Software performance doesn't stop at the application layer. Understanding OSI Layer 3 through Layer 7 routing, TCP window scaling, and DNS propagation changes the way you write backend code.\n\n### Core Concepts:\n- **TCP Three-Way Handshake & Keep-Alives**: How persistent HTTP/2 and connection reuse cut latency by over 60%.\n- **Subnetting & VPC Isolation**: Protecting database clusters with private subnets and security group ingress rules.\n- **Bufferbloat & MTU Sizing**: Why packet fragmentation causes subtle timeout issues in high-throughput microservices.\n\nA disciplined network perspective ensures that backend services remain resilient even under challenging network conditions.",
    "created_at": "2026-09-17T12:44:18.073Z"
  }
},
